From dfaa3a7190f534a596b4b2b1fa0a52eac856a7cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hang(Harry) Gao <GaohRyan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 03:18:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] opt: anchor_obs_mode=ori (reference anchor orientation
 only, no position)

With env.anchor_obs on, env.anchor_obs_mode selects what the actor gets about the
reference anchor: full = position (3) + rot6d (6) as before; ori = rot6d (6) only.
The orientation term needs an IMU-level estimate; the position term needs global
localisation. Default full: existing configs and checkpoints behave as before.
Goal width 689 (full) / 686 (ori). Imagination slices the same analytic term.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
